From 0030905473103151286278370f5b85f5001343ff Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kelvin Lee <kelvin.cushman@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 00:12:40 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(rebrand): close the gaps the Orphus rebrand patch left
 against upstream gates

The rebrand renamed identifiers, env vars, and config dirs but missed the
repo's own enforcement surfaces. All four test suites (unit, integration,
ci-contracts) and biome/typecheck/shrinkwrap now pass.

- config: getAgentDirs() now includes the fork-legacy ~/.atomic/agent tier,
  honoring the promised .orphus -> .atomic -> .pi fallback for discovery,
  settings, and extensions
- startup: first-run setup is skipped when settings.json exists in any
  config-dir tier, so existing Atomic installs are not re-onboarded (this
  also unblocks terminal startup under the engine test harness)
- workflows: relative global workflow paths resolve against the agent dir
  whose config.json declared them (new resolvedGlobalWorkflows on
  ConfigLoadResult, threaded into toScopedDiscoveryConfig); raw configs
  stay untouched for provenance
- ci: rename ATOMIC_REQUIRE_*_SMOKE workflow env vars to ORPHUS_* to match
  renamed consumers and the CI topology contract
- changelogs: restore released sections to their at-tag content; released
  history is immutable and keeps its ATOMIC_* wording
- lockfile: add the roundtable workspace to package-lock.json (npm ci was
  failing), regenerate npm-shrinkwrap for the orphus bin, drop the
  bun.lock the rebrand patch reintroduced
- tests: derive expected paths from CONFIG_DIR_NAME instead of hardcoded
  .atomic; follow the guide command rename to /orphus; biome import-order
  fixes for renamed ORPHUS_* identifiers
